{
	"info": {
		"name": "08 · Live scenarios",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
		"description": "Narrative happy-path walkthroughs for **frontend devs**: run top-to-bottom and watch the end-to-end story — a stateless chat, a persisted red-team conversation, authoring, flagging, and review. Assertions stay light; the story is the point.\n\n**Runs green unattended, real replies when you set a key.** The model is registered with a credential **only when `live_model_key` is set** (prerequest-built body). Without it, the SSE steps carry an `error` event (still HTTP 200, turns persist) — so the whole suite passes unattended; set `live_model_key` (env `local`, e.g. an OpenRouter `sk-or-...`) to see real generations. Default wiring: OpenRouter via the `generic` provider (`live_provider`/`live_model_id`/`live_endpoint` override it).\n\n**Auth model.** Per-request `{{admin_token}}` throughout; folder E's reviewer uses `{{annotator_token}}` (the seeded `annotator` — no manual verify-token step). Self-contained — no `00-bootstrap`.\n\n**Run order:** Setup → A → B → C → D → E → Teardown (B's conversation feeds D, D's flag feeds E). A fresh group is `pending_approval`; folder B approves it before adding evaluations (C reuses that approved group).\n\n**SSE note:** the chat + message endpoints return `text/event-stream`; the assertions here are transport-level (HTTP status + persistence), and the Postman GUI renders the stream.\n\n**Leftovers.** The evaluation group leaks (no group DELETE; `run_suffix`-unique); the seeded annotator is left intact. Everything else is torn down.\n\n**Verified:** 48/48 checks green end-to-end against a live stack, no key needed (`make up` + `make seedlocal`); real replies verified separately with a live `live_model_key`."
	},
